    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δνοφ-ερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dark, murky,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.269
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				243
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχλύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					379
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ δ. γᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1266
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κᾶδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.112
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					536
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).—Poet. word; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δνοφερόν</span>”
				<i>gloom,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			.</div>
